get.description:
Return the current social_onboarding_state map for the authenticated user.

Response: { "data": { "social_onboarding_state": <map or null> } }

Auth: Bearer token.

delete.description:
Delete multiple Facebook posts (scheduled or published) for a page.

Body:
    {
        "post_ids": ["post_id1", "post_id2"]
    }

patch.description:
Update Facebook page status / enable flag.

Request Body:
    {
        "status": "READY|VERIFYING|VERIFICATION_FAILED|UNVERIFIED",
        "is_enable": true
    }

get.description:
Get the original input (caption, image, template) for a batch.

Returns:
    { caption, image_url, template_id, created_at }

delete.description:
Remove one translation from an ad template's group. The original
can't be removed through this route — use DELETE /ads/templates/{id}
instead.

OnboardingAdAccountItem.description:
A single existing Meta ad account offered to the user on the Setup step.

``id`` is Ally's internal ad-account id (the one the select endpoint takes);
``meta_ad_account_id`` is the Meta ``act_…`` id shown for reference.

UpdateNotificationSettingsRequest.description:
Request payload for updating notification settings.

`notification_email`/`notification_phone` of None means "leave as is";
an empty/whitespace string means "clear it".
